\f1 \cf2 \ul What
\f0 \ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl313\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 They propose a model that produces cultural differentiation based only on social cognition and does not require a segregated network or a preexisting division into groups. They called it 
\f2\b associative diffusion
\f1\b0 , and use two insights from cognition: 1. 
\f2\b Cognitive association
\f1\b0  between concepts (like a network in which a concept is linked to another if they are associated in some way), and 2. 
\f2\b constrain satisfaction
\f1\b0  (in simple words, they constantly search for congruency between our associations, and if a new exposure to a behavior changes our perception in a direction that it\'92s incongruent with our prior, that\'92s dropped.)
\f0 \

\f1 They critique that in models like DellaPosta 2015, the cultural differentiation is ultimately epiphenomenal to a structurally segmented world. Also, these models do not require any homophilous interaction (the interactions -see the behavior of a random person- are random too.)
\f0 \

\f1 Quotes: 1. Culture is often measured as the distribution of beliefs in a population. A consistent finding in the sociology of culture is that beliefs are not randomly distributed. (Martin 2002).
